  "id": "dichromatism",
  "term": "dichromatism",
  "definition": "Dichromatism is a form of abnormal colour vision in which the range of colour differences a person can perceive is effectively reduced to two basic colour components instead of the fuller normal range. In this older usage, it refers to a partial colour-blindness affecting how the spectrum is distinguished.",
